# Per-machine paths. Copy this file to  tools\local.paths.txt  and edit it.
#
# local.paths.txt is gitignored, so every PC that clones this repo keeps its own copy
# and nothing machine-specific is ever committed. You usually do NOT need it: the
# packagers and harnesses call tools\Find-KCD2.ps1, which finds a Steam install on its
# own, including libraries on a second drive. Use this file when it cannot - a
# non-Steam copy (Epic, GOG), an unusual folder, or a separate dev build.
#
# The environment variables KCD2_DIR and KCD2_DEV_DIR override this file.

# The game you play. Must be the folder that contains Bin\ , Data\ and Mods\ .
# game=D:\Games\Steam\steamapps\common\KingdomComeDeliverance2

# The modding/dev build, used ONLY by PackageModDev.bat. This is the build that writes
# kcd.log with [Error]/[Warning] lines naming the exact Skald node that failed; the
# retail build swallows them silently. It is never auto-detected and never guessed from
# the retail path, because deploying a dev pak into the game you actually play is worse
# than failing - so if you want PackageModDev.bat, set this.
# dev=D:\Games\Steam\steamapps\common\KCD2Mod
